{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-45-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧, like thirsty dogs (Paley), cf. 131. ⟦2⟧. ⟦3⟧ corresponding to ⟦4⟧, but this receives a new finite verb with ⟦5⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-2-mentioned1", "translation": "you licked"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-2-mentioned2", "translation": "and libations"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-2-mentioned3", "translation": "and meals"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-2-mentioned4", "translation": "they sacrificed"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ the scholiast explains: ⟦2⟧, and better still ⟦3⟧. 469 ff. (only water and honey; 481 ⟦4⟧); see also the scholia on this."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-3-mentioned1", "translation": "wineless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-3-mentioned2", "translation": "for wine is not poured to the Erinyes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-3-mentioned3", "translation": "nor to offer wine"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ ⟦2⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-4-mentioned1", "translation": "soothing offerings"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ with the final syllables as a resolved arsis, like ⟦2⟧ 797, ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧. (other examples in Paley on V. 797)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-5-mentioned1", "translation": "wineless offerings"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-5-mentioned2", "translation": "witnesses were present"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-5-quote1", "translation": "Hermes of the underworld, ancestral, etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-6-comment1", "translation": "108 ⟦1⟧ is surely one word, like ⟦2⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-6-mentioned1", "translation": "night-revered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-6-mentioned2", "translation": "night-wandering, night-roaming, night-watched"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-7-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ can and will be a separate altar here (⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧; see also ⟦4⟧), which could easily be set up for the purpose; but the special thing is the hour (Schol. ⟦5⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-7-mentioned1", "translation": "hearth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-7-mentioned2", "translation": "hearth of Phoebus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-7-mentioned3", "translation": "at midnight they begin the offerings to the Erinyes alone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (and ⟦2⟧) in the time expression always thus in the accusative, ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧, Aristot. ⟦5⟧. ⟦6⟧. 30 end ⟦7⟧, Gramm. of New Testament Greek § 34, 8 p. 97² (= ⟦8⟧, at the hour)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned1", "translation": "hour"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned2", "translation": "untimely hour"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned3", "translation": "Pol."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned4", "translation": "Ath."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned5", "translation": "the hour that had been announced"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-mentioned6", "translation": "at the hour"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-45-8-quote1", "translation": "the appointed hour"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧ 112 as at 627.904? ⟦4⟧? (Kühner-Gerth I, 68 note, II, 247); according to ordinary usage ⟦5⟧ should follow."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-1-mentioned1", "translation": "trampled underfoot"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-1-mentioned2", "translation": "and these things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-1-mentioned3", "translation": "having rushed"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ ⟦2⟧ (⟦3⟧ M.). ⟦4⟧; cf. ⟦5⟧ Xen. Kyneg. 6, 6."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-2-mentioned1", "translation": "net-setter"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-2-mentioned2", "translation": "net-setting"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ Schol. ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧; Hesych. ⟦4⟧, from ⟦5⟧ (⟦6⟧), to make distorted eyes; also ⟦7⟧ ⟦8⟧, where ⟦9⟧ is transmitted."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned1", "translation": "having cast a sidelong glance"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned2", "translation": "having mocked"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned3", "translation": "having laughed at"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned4", "translation": "to cast a sidelong glance, to mock"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned5", "translation": "squinting, to squint"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned6", "translation": "to squint"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-46-3-mentioned7", "translation": "having cast a sidelong glance well"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: is ambiguous: \"as\" and \"while\", \"since\", like ⟦2⟧ and often; the latter seems preferable. ⟦3⟧ like Homer ⟦4⟧ (Χ 161), ⟦5⟧ (⟦6⟧ 422), and ⟦7⟧ with ⟦8⟧, etc. (see Paley), everywhere \"for life\", which does not exactly fit here; also Kl. is a mere ⟦9⟧. But the sense is similarly strong."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned1", "translation": "as"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned2", "translation": "of my life"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned3", "translation": "running for life"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned4", "translation": "as for life"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned5", "translation": "i"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned6", "translation": "contest"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-1-mentioned7", "translation": "life"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ \"understand, take to heart\", cf. ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-2-mentioned1", "translation": "take thought"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-2-mentioned2", "translation": "I know, I think"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ see above p. 81; ⟦2⟧ with the false ⟦3⟧ is also in M. here. The name is meant to bring to consciousness."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-3-mentioned1", "translation": "dream"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-3-mentioned2", "translation": "Clytemnestra"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-47-3-mentioned3", "translation": "n"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-comment1", "translation": "Distichomythia on the part of Kl.; the chorus likewise symmetrically first twice ⟦1⟧, then twice ⟦2⟧, finally, what Hermann calls epodic, ⟦3⟧ and after that ⟦4⟧ etc. The interjections are indicated by ⟦5⟧ (Schol.); such a thing occurs (Weckl.) among the tragedians now only here, in Aristophanes more often. ⟦6⟧ Arist. ⟦7⟧. 10. Thesm. 231 (sound of pain; in the Th. follows ⟦8⟧, cf. ⟦9⟧ likewise ⟦10⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned1", "translation": "mu"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned2", "translation": "oh"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned3", "translation": "mu mu"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned4", "translation": "take"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned5", "translation": "stage direction"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned6", "translation": "Mu mu"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned7", "translation": "Hipp."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned8", "translation": "why do you moan?"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-48-1-mentioned9", "translation": "they moan"}]}